# Enforce consistent line endings so tools (editors, sed, AI assistants) can't
# flip them and create whole-file line-ending churn in diffs.
#
# "text eol=crlf" stores the blob normalized (LF) in the repo but checks the file
# out as CRLF in the working tree. Because git compares the normalized form,
# a tool that writes LF (or CRLF) produces no diff at all - the flip-flop stops.

# Arduino source + project docs: CRLF working tree (project convention)
*.ino   text eol=crlf
*.h     text eol=crlf
*.md    text eol=crlf

# Python tooling (test harnesses): LF
*.py    text eol=lf
